On level 7, my chaotic monk found an altar to Huan Ti, no priest, but
still a good thing, especially since I was carrying a Bag of Tricks. So
naturally, I started pulling critters out of the bag. First pull: seven
hill orcs. Slip into the corridor, let them come to me, and they went down
in a trice. The cat ate one, but three went to the god; clovers every
time. Now the cat's stuck in the corridor for the second pull: acid blob,
no corpse. Then on the third pull, five more hill orcs, leaving two
corpses and two more clovers. That was it, the bag was empty already. BUt
along comes a leprechaun, and begorra, another clover. How appropriate.
Then off a giant bat that took me down to 1/3hp, I heard "Use thy gift
wisely," and looked down to see... Stormbringer. I used my gift of
*wisdom* and didn't call Huan Ti any malevolent names for giving a monk a
broadsword. If I die, I'll play a ranger next game in the hope of finding
the bones file.

But having gotten six bumps of luck and an artifact out of the deal, I
couldn't complain much anyway, right? Next level was oracle; having not
done the mines I didn't have naything to bust the statues with, so off to
Soko! Zot! A level teleport trap. Ah boo. Now my cat is six levels away
and I have to reach her fast. 

But on the way down I'm feeling lucky, right? I've just gotten what, +6 or
so to my luck and Huan TI is pleased as punch with me (or so I'd guess),
so I can't help stopping at a water fountain and hoping for a little
boost. 

Uh-oh, water demon. And he just summoned his brother. And the stairs down
are on the other side of the dungeon. Run as fast as I can and --oops--
there's a giant bat in front of me. Whomp whomp: killed by a giant bat on
level... three!? (&*Rassafargin arglebargle RNG....*%)

